Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:26:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 33/39] drama: tf-drama-reference-prefill runs the backbone
 over voice-reference rows

The rows are staged as drama_host.zig stages them, at chunk sizes 1, 7 and 128,
and after a reset. The final-norm hidden of every row and the last row's
semantic logits are written in tf-drama-backbone-oracle's file layout, so a
native-against-reference prefill comparison can read them. Building it runs no
GPU.
